  <prompt>Reconcile the three misalignments discovered during first live batch dispatch attempt of task 186 (2026-08-26 SESSION 13):

**Discovery 1 — Task 023 script never deployed**: TASK-INDEX marked task 023 ✅ (2bfd64dfa 2026-08-17) authoring `scripts/Extend-DataverseEnvironmentSchema-v3.3.ps1` but the script was never executed against any env. Verified via raw Dataverse Web API query to `spaarkedev1.crm.dynamics.com/api/data/v9.2/EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='sprk_dataverseenvironment')/Attributes` — returned original 17 columns only, none of the 12 v3.3 additions. Task 023 ✅ status reflects code-authoring only, not deployment.

**Discovery 2 — Missing 13th column sprk_customerid**: Task 023 POML enumerated 12 columns but NONE was `sprk_customerid` — the ALT-KEY that L2 `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Concurrency/DataverseRegistryConcurrencyStore.cs` and `CustomerRunGuard.cs` require for every registry lookup (`$filter=sprk_customerid eq '{id}'`). Grep across `src/**` confirmed the column is expected by L2 code but has no source-side authoring anywhere. Real gap in task 023's enumeration.

**Discovery 3 — Skill drift in `/provision-environment` Step 1f + Step 6a + Fallback Matrix**: skill payload referenced 3 fields that don't exist anywhere in code, POMLs, script, or live schema: `sprk_profile`, `sprk_upgrademode`, and used string 'Provisioning' + integer 200000004 for `sprk_setupstatus` — actual enum is `NotStarted=0/InProgress=1/Ready=2/Issue=3` (per `DataverseEnvironmentRecord.cs:23-29`). Payload also omitted 5 required NOT-NULL fields (`sprk_name`, `sprk_environmenttype`, `sprk_dataverseurl`, `sprk_isactive`, `sprk_isdefault`) — Dataverse would 400 on missing required attrs.

Together these three block ANY live dispatch of task 186 (interactive OR batch). Fix all three atomically.</prompt>

  <role>Main-session operator (Sub-Agent Write Boundary applies: SKILL.md edits main-session-only). Author for durability — this reconciliation ships the schema state that r1's L2 code has been assuming since 2026-08-17 but was never actually deployed.</role>

  <goal>By session end: (1) spaarkedev1 has all 12 task-023 columns + `sprk_customerid` + alt-key deployed; (2) `.claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md` Step 1f + Step 6a + Fallback Matrix reference only fields that ACTUALLY exist in the deployed schema with correct enum integers; (3) task 186 batch dispatch can proceed cleanly on next session's re-invocation.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The 2026-08-26 SESSION 13 first live batch dispatch of task 186 stopped at Step 0 pre-Step-0.5 with three cascading discoveries:

      1. **pac + MCP env-pointer confusion** — initially pointed at `spaarke-model1-prod` (customer stamp from 2026-08-22 stand-up), operator directed to use `spaarkedev1` as the registry env (since no separate central-managing env exists yet — see operator memory `feedback_no_central_managing_env_yet`).

      2. **Task 023 script deployment gap** — after switching to spaarkedev1, MCP describe still showed 17 columns. Verified via raw Web API: script authoring committed (`2bfd64dfa`) but never executed against any env.

      3. **sprk_customerid missing entirely** — L2 CustomerRunGuard `DataverseRegistryConcurrencyStore.CustomerIdColumn = "sprk_customerid"` (line 60) is the alt-key for every registry lookup. Grep across all r1 tasks + all scripts confirmed NO authoring of this column anywhere. Real gap in task 023's enumeration.

      4. **Skill drift** — SKILL.md Step 1f payload referenced `sprk_profile` + `sprk_upgrademode` (grep-zero across `src/**` — both fields fictional) + used wrong `sprk_setupstatus` values.

      The reconciliation is fully executed in this task; POML authored post-hoc to document scope + close the gap in TASK-INDEX + surface for the next audit.
